{
  "description": "What the HTTP destination sends to a local receiver and the result it returns. settings are overrides of the settings of the destination (the url is the local receiver, which the test fills in); the receiver answers server_status; expected_body is the exact canonical batch body (decompressed when the request says Content-Encoding: gzip); expected_headers are headers the request must carry; expected_no_request means the receiver must get no request. The result: events below the minimum severity count as accepted; a 2xx accepts the sent events; 408, 429 and 5xx fail them (transient, reason status_<code>); any other status drops them (permanent, reason status_<code>).",
